"**Header:**\n\u2022 Patient: Alex  \n\u2022 Visit type: Telehealth consult  \n\n---\n\n**S - Subjective:**\n\u2022 CC: 4-day hx feeling \u201cunder the weather\u201d  \n\u2022 HPI:\n  \u2022 Onset 4 days ago after colleague with frequent sneezing at work (possible exposure from colleague\u2019s children in kindergarten)  \n  \u2022 Initial sore throat + runny nose \u2192 sore throat now improving  \n  \u2022 Sore throat: very painful x 1\u20132 days, painful swallowing; did not look in throat; no reported white spots/redness (not assessed)  \n  \u2022 Nasal sx: started runny, now mostly congestion; nose \u201cstuffed all the time\u201d  \n  \u2022 Cough: started yesterday, dry, non-pleuritic, constant, not worse at any particular time  \n  \u2022 Night sweats x ~3\u20134 days, causing tiredness/uneasy feeling  \n  \u2022 Fever at onset, now settling with paracetamol and ibuprofen  \n  \u2022 Dyspnea: feels \u201cwinded\u201d/SOB on exertion, none at rest; stopped going to gym; still able to go to work  \n  \u2022 No chest pain  \n  \u2022 Ears: no pain, no blockage, no discharge  \n  \u2022 Headache: intermittent, generalized; no visual disturbance, no photophobia  \n  \u2022 No nausea or vomiting  \n  \u2022 Bowels OK  \n  \u2022 Passing urine OK  \n  \u2022 Appetite slightly \u2193; drinking more than usual  \n  \u2022 No rashes  \n  \u2022 Myalgia/joint aches started in past couple of days  \n\u2022 PMH:\n  \u2022 Otherwise fit and well; no ongoing medical problems reported  \n\u2022 Meds:\n  \u2022 Paracetamol (for fever)  \n  \u2022 Ibuprofen (for fever)  \n\u2022 Allergies:\n  \u2022 NKDA  \n\u2022 FH:\n  \u2022 Grandmother: DM type 2  \n  \u2022 Great-grandfather: eczema  \n\u2022 SH:\n  \u2022 Lives alone  \n  \u2022 Occupation: accountant; currently busy/stressful year-end period; feels slightly slower at work due to illness  \n  \u2022 Mood: enjoys job; no significant mood concerns; considers stress \u201cgood kind\u201d  \n  \u2022 Smoking: occasional cigars at company parties (not regular)  \n  \u2022 Alcohol: occasional, not heavy  \n\n---\n\n**O - Objective:**\n\u2022 No in-consult exam or vitals documented (telehealth history only)  \n\n---\n\n**A - Assessment:**\n1. Viral URTI / possible early influenza  \n   \u2022 4-day hx sore throat (improving), nasal congestion, new dry cough, initial fever responding to paracetamol/ibuprofen, myalgia, intermittent headache, night sweats, mild exertional SOB, ongoing function preserved  \n2. Exertional SOB in context of acute viral illness  \n   \u2022 SOB only on exertion, none at rest; no chest pain, able to work; likely due to current viral infection but needs safety-netting  \n\n---\n\n**P - Plan:**\n\u2022 Viral URTI / possible early flu:\n  \u2022 Advise rest; recommend 1\u20132 days off work  \n  \u2022 Encourage oral fluids; maintain good hydration  \n  \u2022 Continue paracetamol and/or ibuprofen as needed for fever and aches (within usual dosing limits \u2013 implied by \u201cregular\u201d)  \n  \u2022 Expect illness course ~7\u201310 days with gradual improvement  \n  \u2022 Review if not better by next week  \n\n\u2022 Exertional SOB / safety-netting:\n  \u2022 Monitor symptoms closely  \n  \u2022 Urgent review/earlier contact if:\n    \u2022 High fever recurs or worsens  \n    \u2022 Breathing becomes more laboured  \n    \u2022 New or worsening chest pain  \n    \u2022 General condition deteriorates  \n\n\u2022 Follow-up:\n  \u2022 Return/phone consult next week if no improvement or sooner per red-flag symptoms above  \n  \u2022 Offer future review for mood/stress if needed (per doctor\u2019s invitation)"